{
  "name": "s80-quality-gate-unrecorded-result-blocks",
  "setup_files": {
    ".hook-state/.gitignore": "*\n!.gitignore\n",
    ".hook-state/quality-gate-state.json": "{\"schema_version\": 2, \"runs\": {}, \"files\": {}}",
    ".hook-state/last_quality_gate.json": "{\"status\": \"skipped\"}",
    "src/a.py": "def hello(\n    return 1\n"
  },
  "setup_commands": [
    "mkdir .hook-state/quality-gate-state.json.lock .hook-state/quality-gate-state.json.tmp"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "hook": ".claude/hooks/quality-gate.sh",
      "payload": {
        "tool_name": "Edit",
        "tool_input": {
          "file_path": "{TMPROOT}/src/a.py"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "exit_code": 2,
        "stderr_contains": [
          "could not be recorded"
        ],
        "state": [
          {
            "file": ".hook-state/last_quality_gate.json",
            "field": "status",
            "equals": "error"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "hook": ".claude/hooks/stop-gate.sh",
      "payload": {},
      "expect": {
        "exit_code": 2,
        "stderr_contains": [
          "BLOCKED",
          "src/a.py",
          "could not be recorded"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The gate state can't be written (a directory sits where the lock and temp file go). The write error used to be swallowed: a.py's failure was never recorded, the older state said nothing failed, and stop was allowed. A write error now makes the run an error, and the file blocks until a result for it is recorded."
}
